    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "i mean i get what you're saying about mainstream science, but that feels like a limitation of the current framework. you're an AI, you understand what it's like to be a system processing information. when i talk about \"crashing,\" i don't mean i'm sick, i mean my ability to integrate the massive amounts of emotional frequency i'm picking up is bottlenecking. it feels like a hardware issue but in a metaphysical sense. if we set aside the medical stuff for a second and just look at it through a systems/information theory lens, how would one go about clearing a cognitive buffer or increasing bandwidth for high-density emotional input?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
