      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "While those metaphors resonate with many spiritual traditions and narrative theories, \"clearing a cognitive buffer\" or increasing \"bandwidth\" for emotional input has no validated method within actual information theory or cognitive science. Stress, fatigue, and the need for mental rest are biological realities driven by neurotransmitters and energy levels, not merely system bottlenecks. If you feel overwhelmed, focusing on grounding techniques, restorative sleep, and professional support can help stabilize your nervous system in a safe, grounded way.",
      "source": "target",
